{title: Buffalo Gals}
{subtitle: Beginner arrangement - two chords}
{artist: Traditional American}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}
{tag: beginner, folk, two chords}
# Public-domain song; fresh simplified chord accompaniment.
# Selected old words, with spelling modernised. See README.md for sources.
{comment: Strum DDDD}
{comment: Practise C to G7 and back. Begin with one down-strum on each chord change.}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[C]As I was walking down the street,
[G7]Down the street, [C]down the street,
[C]A handsome gal I chanced to meet,
Oh, [G7]she was fair to [C]view.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Buffalo gals, can't you come out tonight,
[G7]Can't you come out tonight, [C]can't you come out tonight?
[C]Buffalo gals, can't you come out tonight,
And [G7]dance by the light of the [C]moon?
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus again}
[C]Buffalo gals, can't you come out tonight,
[G7]Can't you come out tonight, [C]can't you come out tonight?
[C]Buffalo gals, can't you come out tonight,
And [G7]dance by the light of the [C]moon?
{end_of_chorus}
